# GitHub Actions hardening

Use when writing or reviewing workflows, especially ones that run agents.

## Permissions
- Set `permissions:` at the top of every workflow, starting from `contents: read`, and grant more per job only where needed.
- Use OIDC (`id-token: write`) to get short-lived cloud credentials instead of long-lived secrets.

## Third-party actions
Pin actions to a full commit SHA (with the version in a comment), and review what they do. Tags can be moved. Let Dependabot propose updates.

## Triggers
- `pull_request_target` and `workflow_run` run with secrets on code from forks. Never check out and run the PR's code in them.
- For `issue_comment` and similar triggers, check `author_association` before doing anything privileged. This matters most for AI agents that anyone can trigger with a comment.

## Injection
Never interpolate untrusted input (`github.event.issue.title`, branch names, PR bodies) directly into `run:` scripts. Pass it through `env:` and quote it.

## Secrets
Scope secrets to environments with required reviewers for production. Do not echo secrets, and avoid `set -x` in steps that use them.

## Verify
Run `forge shield` (it has CI rules for these cases) and `actionlint`. Check that fork PRs cannot reach secrets.
